# 15. Important health-language rules

Use neutral, respectful wording.

Do not:

* Diagnose users
* Guarantee weight loss or gain
* Claim BMI measures body fat
* Call the reference range a perfect or mandatory weight
* Present sugar limits as required intake
* Describe automatically generated meals as medically prescribed
* Claim that 1 kg/week is appropriate for everyone
* Claim automatic Calo synchronization

Use language such as:

* Estimate
* Reference range
* General wellness
* Screening measure
* Upper limit
* Illustrative plan
* Consult a qualified professional when needed

